.Dd August 16, 2026
.Dt ACPI_APPLE 4 amd64
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm acpi_apple
.Nd Apple platform ACPI driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd device acpi_apple
.Cd device backlight
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver attaches to Apple platform ACPI devices found on Intel-based
Macs and provides two independent functions through a single driver,
selected by the ACPI hardware ID it matches:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It APP9876 , APP000B
Platform instance.
Attaches to the PCH PMC companion
.Pq T2 Macs, 2018 and later
or the GMUX GPU multiplexer companion
.Pq Intel Macs with discrete graphics, 2006-2020 .
Arms Wake-on-LAN on shutdown for any interface with wake enabled
.Pq e.g. Va dev.bge.N.wake=1 ,
and follows the ACPI lid switch, blanking the backlight when the lid is
closed and restoring it when the lid is reopened.
.It APP0002
Backlight instance.
Controls the panel backlight found on all Intel Macs with an internal
display, and registers with the
.Xr backlight 9
framework.
The correct control method is selected automatically.
.El
.Pp
.Dv APP0001
.Pq SMC companion
is intentionally not claimed by this driver; it is owned by
.Xr asmc 4 .
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver supports the Apple ACPI devices found in the DSDT of Intel-based
Macs:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
APP9876, the PCH PMC companion, present on T2 Macs
.Pq 2018 and later .
.It
APP000B, the GMUX GPU multiplexer, present on Intel Macs with discrete
graphics
.Pq 2006-2020 ,
including single-GPU Mac minis.
.It
APP0002, the panel backlight, present on all Intel Macs with a built-in
display.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr acpi 4 ,
.Xr asmc 4 ,
.Xr backlight 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
